    "extraction_notes": [
      "Forward and reverse curves were digitized from the supplied plots without adding interpolated points; the grouped curves explicitly include DSK16.",
      "Fig. 3 DSK16-DSK18 curve is a typical forward curve at Tj=25 degC, pulse width=300 us, and 1% duty cycle; its y-axis is logarithmic and its plotted current is instantaneous forward current.",
      "Fig. 4 DSK12-DSK16 solid curves show instantaneous reverse-current magnitude versus percent of rated peak reverse voltage at Tj=25 degC and Tj=100 degC; plotted reverse-current polarity is represented as positive magnitude.",
      "The electrical-characteristics table gives IR1 maximum 0.2 mA for the DSK12-DSK16 group at VR=VDC and TA=25 degC. The separate IR2 high-temperature maximum is 20 mA for the DSK12-DSK16 group at VR=VDC and TA=100 degC; it is not used as the reverse-current fit target.",
      "Absolute-rating bounds for DSK16 are VRRM=60 V, VRMS=42 V, VDC=60 V, IF(AV)=1.0 A, and IFSM=25 A at TA=25 degC; these are limits, not fitted curve points. Source: p. 1 maximum ratings.",
      "The datasheet publishes no reverse-recovery-time specification and no breakdown-voltage or breakdown-current specification; VRRM/VDC ratings are not treated as breakdown data.",
